What the USB port does when it dies after a reboot
==================================================

Captured from /proc/last_kmsg on the Fold 5 (SM-F946B), read over adb on
2026-09-27. The phone's own boot reason for that boot was 'reboot' and
/sys/fs/pstore was empty, so this is not a panic: the kernel stayed up and the
USB controller spun. The full 7821-line capture is 823KB of mostly the same four
lines; an unedited copy is on the phone at
/sdcard/Download/dsh-agent/usb-otg-pwr-event-storm.log and on the machine that
captured it. This is the part that carries the meaning.

The signature, repeated 1342 times between t=2112.7s and t=2630.9s of that boot
- eight and a half minutes of it, roughly two and a half a second:

